    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d611">

                <pb facs="0769" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg757"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/1425a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Standley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-30T18:00:00-04:00">April 30, 1943—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>268. “From Spalding for Burns. It would appear most desirable to ferry as many
                    airplanes as possible via Alaska, in view of the great saving of time in
                    delivery and the difficulties (including effort to disassemble and assemble) of
                    shipping by water. In formulating <pb facs="0770" n="758" xml:id="pg758"/>
                    plans, it would be very helpful to have information regarding future planned
                    capacity of the route and possibility of expansion.”<anchor n="94"
                        xml:id="d611-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d611-f1" n="94" xml:id="d611-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence on the question of the use of the Alaska–Siberia route for
                    ferrying airplanes and as an improved means of communications, see <ref
                        target="#pg616">pp. 616</ref>–<ref target="#pg723">723</ref>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">passim.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
